# Forest-grown beech (Fagus sylvatica) for the Poseidon forest (Everon/Malden blocks): the CWA
# beech (tree_str_buk) drawn up to the 25 m of a closed stand. Long clean bole, the crown in the
# upper half, a dense layered canopy (reference: toni-forest f_005 interior, f_013 edge).
# Base species: solstice-cwa-buk.
height 25
trunk radius=0.34 flare=0.5 gnarl=0.04
crown round
bark beech_bark
level per_metre=2.4 span=0.48..0.97 angle=55..30 length=0.36 taper=0.3 radius=0.45 upturn=0.25 droop=0 gnarl=0.2 whorl=0
level per_metre=3.0 span=0.2..1 angle=42..42 length=0.42 taper=0.3 radius=0.6 upturn=0.05 droop=0.05 gnarl=0.35 whorl=0
level per_metre=7 span=0.25..1 angle=35..35 length=0.35 taper=0.3 radius=0.6 upturn=0 droop=0.1 gnarl=0.5 whorl=0
terminal on
leaves broadleaf_leaves per_metre=40 length=0.08..0.12 width=0.6 variants=0.5,0.3,0.15,0.05 normals=0.5
